Rem ==================================================================
Rem seedfintest.shoddy — test program for seedfin.shoddy's day-count
Rem and bond words
Rem
Rem Assert-driven, in the cuttletest / reckonertest / seedtest pattern:
Rem it prints what it is doing and stops the run at the first assertion
Rem that fails, ending with ALL ASSERTIONS PASSED when it does not.
Rem
Rem WHAT IS GRADED HERE. fin.shoddy's own arithmetic has a known-answer
Rem suite of its own (tst/fin.shoddy), and seedfin's rates, time value,
Rem loans and capital budgeting arrived with the first seeding pass.
Rem What is graded here is the second subsystem: the day counts, and
Rem the bond pricer standing on them. THE CALENDAR WORDS MOVED to
Rem seedjulian when the calendar moved to julian.shoddy, and their walk
Rem moved with them to tst/seedjuliantest.shoddy; the dates the bond
Rem words below consume are built by JULDATE, which is why this suite
Rem folds both seeds.
Rem
Rem WHY THE GUARDS MATTER MORE HERE THAN ANYWHERE. Almost nothing in
Rem this subsystem ABORTS on bad input — FinYearFrac falls through to
Rem actual/365.25 for a basis it does not recognise, and FinLastCoupon
Rem steps back by 12/freq months whether or not that is a whole number.
Rem Every one of those is a WRONG ANSWER rather than a refusal, and a
Rem wrong answer about money is the failure this whole seed layer
Rem exists to prevent. So the guard sections below are the point of the
Rem file and not its housekeeping.
Rem
Rem THE ONE ABORT is FinYtm's, when no yield between 0 and 2 prices the
Rem bond, and it is guarded the way FINIRR's twin already is: the same
Rem test asked first, and refused instead.
Rem
Rem Every refusal is walked in the seed suite's two-part shape — the line
Rem refuses for the stated reason with the state as it was, AND a further
Rem line evaluates afterwards.
Rem
Rem Run: bin\mill run tst\seedfintest.shoddy      (from the repo root)
Rem ==================================================================

Include "../machines/cuttle.shoddy"
Include "../machines/reckoner.shoddy"
Include "../machines/seq.shoddy"
Include "../machines/str.shoddy"
Include "../machines/seeds/seedfin.shoddy"
Include "../machines/seeds/seedjulian.shoddy"
Rem Folded only for the fit section below, and onto a state of its own:
Rem a fit is a dict, and DGET is how a session actually reads one, so
Rem reading it any other way would test something nobody types.
Include "../machines/seeds/seeddict.shoddy"

Rem ---- reading an answer ------------------------------------------------

Def Ran(st As RckState, line As String) As RckState
    Select Case RckEval(st, line)
        Case RckNext(st2, out)
            st2
        Case RckStop(st2, why, out)
            st2
        Case Else
            st

Def Bad(st As RckState, line As String) As Boolean
    Select Case RckEval(st, line)
        Case RckStop(st2, why, out)
            True
        Case Else
            False

Def Why(st As RckState, line As String) As String
    Select Case RckEval(st, line)
        Case RckStop(st2, why, out)
            why
        Case Else
            ""

Def Text(st As RckState) As String
    Join(Map(CutCells(RckStack(st)), Fn(c) => CutShow(c, RckFmt(st))), " | ")

Def Deep(st As RckState) As Number
    CutDepth(RckStack(st))

Def TopNum(st As RckState) As Number
    If Deep(st) < 1 Then
        0 - 999999
    Else
        NumOf(First(CutCells(RckStack(st))))

Def NumOf(c As Cell) As Number
    Select Case c
        Case CutNum(x)
            x
        Case Else
            0 - 999999

Def Got(st As RckState, line As String) As Number
    TopNum(Ran(st, line))

Def Tol() As Number
    0.0001

Def Near(a As Number, b As Number) As Boolean
    Abs(a - b) <= Tol()

Def Q(s As String) As String
    Chr(34) & s & Chr(34)

Def Refuses(st As RckState, line As String, part As String) As Boolean
    Bad(st, line) And Instr(Why(st, line), part) > 0 And Text(Ran(st, line)) = Text(st) And Text(Ran(Ran(st, line), "1 1 +")) = Text(Ran(st, "1 1 +"))

Def Holds(lines As List Of String, sub As String) As Boolean
    Any(lines, Fn(l) => Instr(l, sub) > 0)

Rem ---- the bond every price assertion below is about --------------------
Rem Five percent, semiannual, settling 15 January 2025 and maturing
Rem exactly five years later on a coupon date, so the stub is zero and
Rem the arithmetic is checkable by hand: at a yield equal to the coupon
Rem it must price at exactly par.

Def Settle() As String
    "2025 1 15 JULDATE"

Def Maturity() As String
    "2030 1 15 JULDATE"

Rem Both banked in registers by the section below, so the bond's two
Rem dates are one short phrase at every call site rather than two
Rem constructions repeated twenty times.
Def Bond() As String
    Q("S") & " RCL " & Q("M") & " RCL"

Def Main()
    Rem seedjulian folds first, seedfin after — the same order HxFresh
    Rem uses, and the dates every bond line below builds come from it.
    Let s0 = RckSeedFin(RckSeedJulian(RckNew()))
    Let g = Ran(s0, "1 2")

    Print("--- the words are registered, pure, and carry their metadata ---")
    Assert(RckKnows(s0, "FINDAYS360") And RckKnows(s0, "FINDATEDIFF") And RckKnows(s0, "FINYEARFRAC"), "THE DAY COUNTS ARE IN THE DICTIONARY")
    Assert(Not RckKnows(RckSeedFin(RckNew()), "JULDATE"), "AND THE CALENDAR WORDS ARE GONE FROM THIS SEED, NOT ALIASED — THEY ARE SEEDJULIAN'S NOW")
    Assert(RckKnows(s0, "FINBONDPRICE") And RckKnows(s0, "FINYTM") And RckKnows(s0, "FINMDUR"), "AND THE BOND PRICER")
    Assert(RckKnows(s0, "FIN360") And RckKnows(s0, "FINSEMI"), "AND THE BASES AND FREQUENCIES ARE WORDS, NOT NUMBERS TO REMEMBER")
    Assert(All(RckDict(s0), Fn(e) => WordEffect(e) <> "" And WordDesc(e) <> ""), "NO WORD IS WITHOUT AN EFFECT LINE AND A DESCRIPTION")
    Assert(All(RckDict(s0), Fn(e) => Length(RckHelp(s0, WordName(e))) = 3), "AND HELP ANSWERS FOR EVERY ONE OF THEM")
    Rem A calendar reaches no clock and a bond price reads no rate feed:
    Rem every word here is arithmetic over cells already on the stack.
    Assert(All(RckDict(s0), Fn(e) => Not RckTouches(e)), "AND NOTHING IN THE WHOLE SEED TOUCHES THE WORLD")

    Print("--- the day counts, where the whole point is that they disagree ---")
    Assert(Got(s0, "2025 1 1 JULDATE 2025 2 1 JULDATE FINDAYS360") = 30, "JANUARY IS 30 DAYS ON THE 30/360 RULE")
    Assert(Got(s0, "2025 1 1 JULDATE 2026 1 1 JULDATE FINACTUAL FINDATEDIFF") = 365, "AND 2025 IS 365 ACTUAL DAYS")
    Assert(Got(s0, "2025 1 1 JULDATE 2026 1 1 JULDATE FIN360 FINDATEDIFF") = 360, "AND 360 ON THE 30/360 RULE")
    Assert(Near(Got(s0, "2025 1 1 JULDATE 2026 1 1 JULDATE FIN360 FINYEARFRAC"), 1), "A YEAR IS A WHOLE YEAR ON 30/360")
    Assert(Near(Got(s0, "2025 1 1 JULDATE 2026 1 1 JULDATE FIN365 FINYEARFRAC"), 1), "AND ON ACTUAL/365")
    Assert(Not Near(Got(s0, "2025 1 1 JULDATE 2026 1 1 JULDATE FINACTUAL FINYEARFRAC"), 1), "BUT NOT ON ACTUAL/365.25, WHICH IS WHY THE BASIS HAS TO BE SAID")

    Print("--- the day counts' guards ---")
    Rem The date-CONSTRUCTION guards walked here under the old names now
    Rem walk in tst/seedjuliantest.shoddy with the words that own them.
    Rem What must still hold HERE is that a date arriving at a day-count
    Rem word is checked on the way in — a dict can be hand-built, and a
    Rem wrong answer about money is the failure this layer is for.
    Assert(Refuses(g, "{ 1 2 } 2026 1 1 JULDATE FINDAYS360", "NOT A DATE"), "A DICT OF THE WRONG SIZE HANDED TO A DAY COUNT")
    Assert(Refuses(RckSeedDict(g), "{ } " & Q("yr") & " 2025 DPUT " & Q("mon") & " 2 DPUT " & Q("day") & " 30 DPUT 2026 1 1 JULDATE FINACTUAL FINDATEDIFF", "THERE IS NO DAY 30"), "AND A HAND-BUILT DICT NAMING A DAY THAT DOES NOT EXIST")
    Assert(Refuses(g, "2025 1 1 JULDATE 2026 1 1 JULDATE 9 FINYEARFRAC", "NOT A DAY-COUNT BASIS"), "A BASIS FIN.SHODDY WOULD HAVE SILENTLY TREATED AS ACTUAL/365.25")
    Assert(Refuses(g, "2025 1 1 JULDATE 2026 1 1 JULDATE 9 FINDATEDIFF", "NOT A DAY-COUNT BASIS"), "AND THE SAME FOR THE DAY COUNT")

    Print("--- the bond, priced against arithmetic that can be done by hand ---")
    Let b = Ran(s0, Settle() & " " & Q("S") & " STO " & Maturity() & " " & Q("M") & " STO")
    Assert(Got(b, Bond() & " FINSEMI FINCOUPONSBEFORE") = 10, "FIVE YEARS OF SEMIANNUAL COUPONS IS TEN OF THEM")
    Assert(Got(b, Bond() & " FINANNUAL FINCOUPONSBEFORE") = 5, "AND FIVE ANNUAL ONES")
    Assert(Text(Ran(b, Bond() & " FINSEMI FINLASTCOUPON JULDATESHOW")) = Q("2025-01-15"), "SETTLING ON A COUPON DATE, THE LAST COUPON IS THAT DAY")
    Rem The assertion the whole pricer turns on: a bond yielding exactly
    Rem its coupon, settling on a coupon date, is worth exactly par. Any
    Rem sign error in the discounting shows up here and nowhere cheaper.
    Assert(Near(Got(b, Bond() & " 0.05 0.05 FINSEMI FIN360 FINBONDPRICE"), 100), "A FIVE PERCENT BOND YIELDING FIVE PERCENT PRICES AT PAR")
    Assert(Got(b, Bond() & " 0.05 0.08 FINSEMI FIN360 FINBONDPRICE") < 100, "A HIGHER YIELD PRICES IT AT A DISCOUNT")
    Assert(Got(b, Bond() & " 0.05 0.02 FINSEMI FIN360 FINBONDPRICE") > 100, "AND A LOWER ONE AT A PREMIUM")
    Rem Price and yield are inverses, so the round trip is the strongest
    Rem check available without a second implementation to compare with.
    Assert(Near(Got(b, Bond() & " 0.05 100 FINSEMI FIN360 FINYTM"), 0.05), "THE YIELD THAT PRICES IT AT PAR IS THE COUPON")
    Assert(Near(Got(b, Bond() & " 0.05 " & Str(Got(b, Bond() & " 0.05 0.08 FINSEMI FIN360 FINBONDPRICE")) & " FINSEMI FIN360 FINYTM"), 0.08), "AND PRICE THEN YIELD ROUND-TRIPS BACK TO THE YIELD IT STARTED FROM")
    Rem Half a year of a five percent coupon on 100 of face is 2.50.
    Assert(Near(Got(b, Q("S") & " RCL 2024 7 15 JULDATE 0.05 FINSEMI FIN360 FINACCRUED"), 2.5), "SIX MONTHS OF A FIVE PERCENT COUPON HAS ACCRUED 2.50 PER 100")
    Assert(Near(Got(b, Q("S") & " RCL " & Q("S") & " RCL 0.05 FINSEMI FIN360 FINACCRUED"), 0), "AND NOTHING HAS ACCRUED ON THE COUPON DATE ITSELF")
    Rem Duration is shorter than maturity for any coupon-paying bond, and
    Rem falls as the yield rises. Both are properties rather than figures,
    Rem which is what a duration can be checked by without a second
    Rem implementation.
    Assert(Got(b, Bond() & " 0.05 0.05 FINSEMI FINMDUR") < 5, "A COUPON BOND'S DURATION IS SHORTER THAN ITS MATURITY")
    Assert(Got(b, Bond() & " 0.05 0.05 FINSEMI FINMDUR") > 4, "AND FOR THIS ONE IT IS OVER FOUR YEARS")
    Assert(Got(b, Bond() & " 0.05 0.09 FINSEMI FINMDUR") < Got(b, Bond() & " 0.05 0.05 FINSEMI FINMDUR"), "AND IT SHORTENS AS THE YIELD RISES")

    Print("--- the bond's guards ---")
    Let bg = Ran(b, "1 2")
    Assert(Refuses(bg, Q("M") & " RCL " & Q("S") & " RCL 0.05 0.05 FINSEMI FIN360 FINBONDPRICE", "SETTLEMENT MUST FALL BEFORE MATURITY"), "A BOND SETTLING AFTER IT MATURES, WHICH WOULD PRICE AN EMPTY COUPON WALK")
    Assert(Refuses(bg, Q("S") & " RCL " & Q("S") & " RCL 0.05 0.05 FINSEMI FIN360 FINBONDPRICE", "SETTLEMENT MUST FALL BEFORE MATURITY"), "AND ONE MATURING THE DAY IT SETTLES")
    Assert(Refuses(bg, Bond() & " 0.05 0.05 5 FIN360 FINBONDPRICE", "MUST DIVIDE 12 EVENLY"), "A COUPON FREQUENCY THAT DOES NOT DIVIDE THE YEAR INTO WHOLE MONTHS")
    Assert(Refuses(bg, Bond() & " 0.05 0.05 0 FIN360 FINBONDPRICE", "MUST DIVIDE 12 EVENLY"), "AND ONE OF ZERO, WHICH WOULD DIVIDE BY IT")
    Assert(Refuses(bg, Bond() & " 0.05 0.05 2.5 FIN360 FINBONDPRICE", "MUST DIVIDE 12 EVENLY"), "AND A FRACTIONAL ONE")
    Assert(Refuses(bg, Bond() & " 0.05 0.05 FINSEMI 9 FINBONDPRICE", "NOT A DAY-COUNT BASIS"), "A BASIS THAT IS NOT ONE")
    Assert(Refuses(bg, Bond() & " 0.05 -2 FINSEMI FIN360 FINBONDPRICE", "HAS NO DISCOUNT FACTOR"), "A YIELD AT MINUS THE FREQUENCY, WHERE THE DISCOUNT BASE IS ZERO")
    Assert(Refuses(bg, Bond() & " 0.05 -3 FINSEMI FIN360 FINBONDPRICE", "HAS NO DISCOUNT FACTOR"), "AND ONE BELOW IT, WHERE THE BASE IS NEGATIVE")
    Rem The one abort in the subsystem, guarded the way FINIRR's is.
    Assert(Refuses(bg, Bond() & " 0.05 5000 FINSEMI FIN360 FINYTM", "NO YIELD BETWEEN 0 AND 2 PRICES THIS BOND"), "A PRICE NO YIELD IN THE BRACKET REACHES, WHICH FINYTM WOULD OTHERWISE ABORT ON")
    Assert(Refuses(bg, "2024 7 15 JULDATE " & Q("S") & " RCL 0.05 FINSEMI FIN360 FINACCRUED", "LAST COUPON MUST FALL ON OR BEFORE SETTLEMENT"), "ACCRUAL RUNNING BACKWARDS FROM A COUPON THAT HAS NOT HAPPENED")
    Assert(Refuses(bg, Bond() & " 0.05 0.05 5 FINMDUR", "MUST DIVIDE 12 EVENLY"), "AND THE SAME FREQUENCY CHECK ON DURATION")

    Print("--- the statistics words are spelled the way fin.shoddy spells them ---")
    Rem Seven of these used to carry an extra S — FINSMEAN for FinMean,
    Rem FINSMIN for FinMinimum — which disambiguated against MEAN and MIN,
    Rem a collision the FIN prefix had already prevented. The rule was also
    Rem applied unevenly: FINSVAR sat beside FINVARP, and FINCORREL never
    Rem took the S though CORREL is taken too. The name is now the
    Rem machine's own, uppercased, and nothing added.
    Assert(RckKnows(s0, "FINMEAN") And RckKnows(s0, "FINVAR") And RckKnows(s0, "FINMEDIAN"), "FINMEAN, FINVAR AND FINMEDIAN ARE THE MACHINE'S OWN NAMES")
    Assert(RckKnows(s0, "FINQUANTILE") And RckKnows(s0, "FINMINIMUM") And RckKnows(s0, "FINMAXIMUM") And RckKnows(s0, "FINRANGEOF"), "AND SO ARE THE OTHER FOUR")
    Assert(Not RckKnows(s0, "FINSMEAN") And Not RckKnows(s0, "FINSVAR") And Not RckKnows(s0, "FINSMEDIAN"), "THE S-FORMS ARE GONE RATHER THAN ALIASED")
    Assert(Not RckKnows(s0, "FINSQUANTILE") And Not RckKnows(s0, "FINSMIN") And Not RckKnows(s0, "FINSMAX") And Not RckKnows(s0, "FINSRANGE"), "AND ALL SEVEN OF THEM ARE")
    Assert(Near(Got(s0, "{ 1 2 3 4 } FINMEAN"), 2.5), "AND THE WORDS STILL ANSWER: THE MEAN")
    Assert(Near(Got(s0, "{ 2 4 4 4 5 5 7 9 } FINVAR"), 32 / 7), "THE SAMPLE VARIANCE, DIVIDING BY N-1")
    Assert(Near(Got(s0, "{ 2 4 4 4 5 5 7 9 } FINVARP"), 4), "AND THE POPULATION ONE BESIDE IT, WHICH NEVER HAD AN S")
    Assert(Near(Got(s0, "{ 3 1 2 } FINMINIMUM"), 1), "THE MINIMUM")
    Assert(Near(Got(s0, "{ 3 1 2 } FINMAXIMUM"), 3), "THE MAXIMUM")
    Assert(Near(Got(s0, "{ 3 1 2 } FINRANGEOF"), 2), "AND THE RANGE BETWEEN THEM")
    Rem Quantile methods differ at the middle and agree at the ends, so the
    Rem ends are what this asserts.
    Assert(Near(Got(s0, "{ 1 2 3 4 } 0 FINQUANTILE"), 1), "THE ZEROTH QUANTILE IS THE SMALLEST VALUE")
    Assert(Near(Got(s0, "{ 1 2 3 4 } 1 FINQUANTILE"), 4), "AND THE FIRST IS THE LARGEST")

    Print("--- FINFITOF: least squares, and the four models by name ---")
    Rem A model is a WORD, as the day-count bases are, so a mistyped one
    Rem is an unknown word rather than a different curve fitted silently.
    Let f0 = RckSeedDict(s0)
    Assert(RckKnows(s0, "FINFITOF"), "THE FIT IS IN THE DICTIONARY")
    Assert(RckKnows(s0, "FINLINEAR") And RckKnows(s0, "FINLOGMODEL") And RckKnows(s0, "FINEXPMODEL") And RckKnows(s0, "FINPOWERMODEL"), "AND ALL FOUR MODELS ARE WORDS, NOT NUMBERS TO REMEMBER")
    Rem y = 2x + 1 exactly, so every one of the three answers is known by
    Rem hand and a sign error anywhere shows up here.
    Assert(Near(Got(f0, "{ 1 2 3 4 } { 3 5 7 9 } FINLINEAR FINFITOF " & Q("slope") & " DGET"), 2), "A STRAIGHT LINE'S SLOPE")
    Assert(Near(Got(f0, "{ 1 2 3 4 } { 3 5 7 9 } FINLINEAR FINFITOF " & Q("intercept") & " DGET"), 1), "ITS INTERCEPT")
    Assert(Near(Got(f0, "{ 1 2 3 4 } { 3 5 7 9 } FINLINEAR FINFITOF " & Q("rfit") & " DGET"), 1), "AND AN EXACT FIT CORRELATES AT ONE")
    Rem y = x^2 through the power model, and y = ln x through the
    Rem logarithmic one: both exact, so both must come back exact.
    Assert(Near(Got(f0, "{ 1 2 4 } { 1 4 16 } FINPOWERMODEL FINFITOF " & Q("slope") & " DGET"), 2), "THE POWER MODEL RECOVERS THE EXPONENT OF y = x^2")
    Assert(Near(Got(f0, "{ 1 2 4 } { 1 4 16 } FINPOWERMODEL FINFITOF " & Q("intercept") & " DGET"), 1), "AND ITS COEFFICIENT")
    Assert(Near(Got(f0, "{ 1 2 4 } { 0 0.6931471805599453 1.3862943611198906 } FINLOGMODEL FINFITOF " & Q("slope") & " DGET"), 1), "THE LOGARITHMIC MODEL RECOVERS y = ln x")
    Assert(Near(Got(f0, "{ 1 2 3 } { 2 4 8 } FINEXPMODEL FINFITOF " & Q("slope") & " DGET"), Log(2)), "AND THE EXPONENTIAL ONE RECOVERS THE RATE OF A DOUBLING")

    Print("--- FINFITOF's guards, including the two fin.shoddy does not state ---")
    Assert(Refuses(g, "{ 1 2 } { 1 2 3 } FINLINEAR FINFITOF", "THEY MUST PAIR UP"), "LISTS OF DIFFERENT LENGTHS, WHICH ZIPWITH WOULD HAVE SILENTLY TRUNCATED")
    Assert(Refuses(g, "{ 1 } { 2 } FINLINEAR FINFITOF", "NEEDS AT LEAST 2 POINTS"), "ONE POINT, WHERE THE VARIANCE DIVIDES BY N-1 AND N IS ONE")
    Assert(Refuses(g, "{ } { } FINLINEAR FINFITOF", "NEEDS AT LEAST 2 POINTS"), "AND NO POINTS AT ALL")
    Assert(Refuses(g, "{ 1 2 3 } { 1 2 3 } 99 FINFITOF", "NOT A MODEL"), "A MODEL NUMBER THAT IS NOT ONE, WHICH FINFITOF WOULD ABORT ON")
    Assert(Refuses(g, "{ 0 1 2 } { 1 2 3 } FINLOGMODEL FINFITOF", "NEEDS EVERY X ABOVE ZERO"), "A LOGARITHMIC FIT THROUGH X = 0")
    Assert(Refuses(g, "{ 1 2 3 } { 0 1 2 } FINEXPMODEL FINFITOF", "NEEDS EVERY Y ABOVE ZERO"), "AN EXPONENTIAL FIT THROUGH Y = 0")
    Assert(Refuses(g, "{ -1 2 3 } { 1 2 3 } FINPOWERMODEL FINFITOF", "NEEDS EVERY X ABOVE ZERO"), "AND A POWER FIT THROUGH A NEGATIVE X")
    Rem The two nobody wrote down: LinFit divides by Var(xs) and Correl
    Rem divides by StdDev(xs) * StdDev(ys), so a list that does not vary
    Rem divides by zero and the runtime ends the session.
    Assert(Refuses(g, "{ 2 2 2 } { 1 2 3 } FINLINEAR FINFITOF", "EVERY X IS THE SAME"), "A VERTICAL LINE, WHICH DIVIDES BY VAR(XS)")
    Assert(Refuses(g, "{ 1 2 3 } { 2 2 2 } FINLINEAR FINFITOF", "EVERY Y IS THE SAME"), "AND A FLAT ONE, WHERE THE CORRELATION DIVIDES BY A SPREAD OF ZERO")
    Assert(Refuses(g, "{ 1 2 3 } " & Q("no") & " FINLINEAR FINFITOF", "needs a LIST, got STRING"), "AND A STRING WHERE THE Y VALUES SHOULD BE")

    Print("--- nothing above cost the session anything ---")
    Assert(Text(Ran(bg, "1 1 +")) = "2 | 2 | 1", "THE STACK IS STILL THERE AND STILL EVALUATING")

    Print("")
    Print("ALL ASSERTIONS PASSED")
